OSD_Process: no <pwd.h>, no user database and no getuid() on wasm32-wasip1.

Two of the three sites EXTEND a condition that is already there, because upstream already excludes
Emscripten from exactly this surface:

  * `#if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)` around `#include <pwd.h>` gains `&& !defined(__wasi__)`
  * UserName()'s `#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)` gains `|| defined(__wasi__)`

Guarding the include alone is what PR #2076 did here, and it left `getpwuid(getuid())` compiling
below it. The call site is guarded too.

The third site, IsSuperUser(), has no condition to extend and gets a new one. getuid() is not
merely unlinkable on WASI: wasi-libc keeps its declaration inside __wasilibc_unmodified_upstream,
so the call does not compile at all.

WHAT THE WASI BRANCH RETURNS:

  * UserName() returns an empty TCollection_AsciiString, which is what the Emscripten arm beside it
    already returns. Both in-tree consumers tolerate that today for that reason: IGESData.cxx:72
    passes it as the default value of the "write.iges.header.author" Interface_Static string, and
    STEPConstruct_AP203Context.cxx:177 uses it to build a person's name. Neither parses it nor
    requires it to be non-empty; an IGES or STEP file written from wasm carries an empty author.
  * IsSuperUser() returns false. A wasip1 instance runs under no user at all, so "not the
    superuser" is the truthful answer rather than a fallback. It has no in-tree caller: measured at
    zero occurrences outside this file.

NOT CHANGED, deliberately: ProcessId() still calls getpid(). wasi-libc declares getpid()
unconditionally and, without -D_WASI_EMULATED_GETPID, only marks it deprecated, so the call
compiles with one warning and needs -lwasi-emulated-getpid at link. The WASI build already carries
that link dependency through wasi-osd-directory.patch's OSD_Directory::BuildTemporary(), so
guarding it here would remove nothing. Both sites are recorded in docs/WASI_GUARD_SITES.md.

Issue: https://github.com/SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift/issues/2173

diff --git a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Process.cxx b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Process.cxx
index dd9bc29e..138d173d 100644
--- a/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Process.cxx
+++ b/src/FoundationClasses/TKernel/OSD/OSD_Process.cxx
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ const OSD_WhoAmI Iam = OSD_WProcess;
   #include <cstdlib>
   #include <sys/param.h>
   #include <sys/time.h>
-  #if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+  #if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) && !defined(__wasi__)
     #include <pwd.h> // For command getpwuid
   #endif
   #include <unistd.h>
@@ -102,8 +102,9 @@ int OSD_Process::ProcessId()
 
 TCollection_AsciiString OSD_Process::UserName()
 {
-  #if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
-  // Emscripten SDK raises TODO exception in runtime while calling getpwuid()
+  #if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__wasi__)
+  // Emscripten SDK raises TODO exception in runtime while calling getpwuid();
+  // wasi-libc has no <pwd.h> and no user database at all
   return TCollection_AsciiString();
   #else
   struct passwd* anInfos = getpwuid(getuid());
@@ -113,7 +114,12 @@ TCollection_AsciiString OSD_Process::UserName()
 
 bool OSD_Process::IsSuperUser()
 {
+  #if defined(__wasi__)
+  // wasi-libc declares no getuid(): a WASI instance runs under no user
+  return false;
+  #else
   return getuid() == 0;
+  #endif
 }
 
